            <ArticleTitle>Herpes zoster vaccine (Zostavax).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>73-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A live attenuated varicella-zoster vaccine (Zostavax--Merck) has been approved by the FDA for prevention of herpes zoster (HZ; zoster; shingles) in persons &gt; or = 60 years old. Each dose of Zostavax contains about 14 times as much varicella-zoster virus (VZV) as Varivax, which has been used in the US since 1995 to vaccinate against varicella (chicken pox).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
